1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,300
Hello, Children's House! I'm Luna. This hour has already started, and it started with joy.

2
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:14,850
I'm Amber, a golden bead! Today your hands will remember what they already know.

3
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:21,880
Look at the room: low shelves, a rug, and work in order. Nobody rushes you here.

4
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:28,670
Three agreements: we walk slowly, we choose one work, and we return it to its place.

5
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:36,970
Put a hand on your chest. Air comes in, air goes out. That is how a lovely hour opens.

6
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:45,780
Clap with me: one, two, and pause. One, two, and pause. Your body learns too.

7
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:51,950
Today we visit hands, senses, words, numbers, the world, and courtesy.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,920
Take a soft step. It is better with an adult nearby. The fun hour is already on its way.

9
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:39,925
Breathe four times, slowly.
Smell an imaginary flower. Blow an imaginary candle.

10
00:01:39,975 --> 00:02:19,930
Walk as if the floor were fine glass.
Heel, toe, heel, toe. Arms stay quiet.

11
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:59,935
The rhythm of the house.
Pat your knees, clap, then silence. Repeat.

12
00:02:59,985 --> 00:03:39,940
Three things you can already do by yourself.
Say them softly: one, two, and three.

13
00:03:39,990 --> 00:04:19,945
One second of a quiet bell.
Close your eyes and listen to the room. Then open them with a smile.

14
00:04:19,995 --> 00:04:59,950
Choose with your eyes.
Look around and point to one work for later. Only one.

15
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:07,270
Practical life: hands care for the house and for themselves. We begin by pouring slowly.

16
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:17,590
The pitcher rises, the water falls, and the glass waits. If it spills, the cloth teaches us. It is not a scolding.

17
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:25,200
Folding is making a tiny bed for the cloth. Corner to corner. The palm smooths.

18
00:05:25,250 --> 00:05:32,980
Buttons ask for patient fingers. The button goes into its round house. You can do it.

19
00:05:33,030 --> 00:05:40,200
A tray is carried with two hands, close to the body. That is how work travels without falling.

20
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:48,260
Watering a plant says: I see you. Just a little water. Then the watering can goes home.

21
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:56,130
Wiping a table gives it its shine back. Small circles. Left to right, unhurried.

22
00:05:56,180 --> 00:06:03,520
The sentence of this house: I can do it by myself. And if I need help, I ask calmly.

23
00:06:03,570 --> 00:07:03,074
Pour in the air.
Imagine the pitcher. Tilt it slowly. Straighten up. Real water only if an adult is with you.

24
00:07:03,124 --> 00:08:02,627
Fold something real.
A napkin, a sock, or a piece of paper. Corner to corner.

25
00:08:02,677 --> 00:09:02,181
Four buttons, four houses.
Fasten four buttons, or gently touch four spots on your clothes.

26
00:09:02,231 --> 00:10:01,735
The invisible tray.
Walk to the door and back, both hands holding the air.

27
00:10:01,785 --> 00:11:01,289
Care for a plant, even a pictured one.
Look at a plant or the picture. Tell it one kind sentence. With a can and an adult, three drops.

28
00:11:01,339 --> 00:12:00,843
The shine of the table.
Move your palm in circles on the table. Then let your hand rest.

29
00:12:00,892 --> 00:13:00,396
Return the work.
If you took something out, put it back in the same place. The shelf smiles when things return.

30
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:59,950
I can.
Say it three times, a little clearer each time: I can do it by myself.

31
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:08,180
The sensorial area sharpens eye, ear, hand, nose, and tongue. Today we play at noticing.

32
00:14:08,230 --> 00:14:16,680
The pink tower goes from large to small. The biggest cube is the base. It never starts at the tip.

33
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:25,850
Color tablets are a family. Red with red. Blue with blue. Your eyes make the introduction.

34
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:35,110
There are loud sounds and soft sounds. A thunder clap, a leaf's whisper. Both deserve silence after.

35
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:42,380
The hand tells rough from smooth. Move your fingers slowly. Name what you feel.

36
00:14:42,430 --> 00:14:51,810
The nose studies too. Cinnamon, lemon, bread, soap. Smell without touching, like a polite guest.

37
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:59,180
The mystery bag hides a shape. The hand guesses: sphere, cube, and nothing in a hurry.

38
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:08,610
When you compare, nobody wins. You only discover: this one is taller, this one is softer, this one is the same.

39
00:15:08,660 --> 00:16:07,527
A tower of cushions.
Order three things from large to small: cushions, cups, or books.

40
00:16:07,577 --> 00:17:06,445
Color hunt.
Find something red, something blue, and something yellow, without running.

41
00:17:06,495 --> 00:18:05,362
Loud and soft.
One loud clap. Then the softest sound you can make. Repeat the pair.

42
00:18:05,412 --> 00:19:04,280
Rough and smooth.
Touch the table, then your cheek. Say which is smoother.

43
00:19:04,330 --> 00:20:03,198
The scientific nose.
Smell your sleeve, a fruit, or the air at the window. Say one word for that smell.

44
00:20:03,248 --> 00:21:02,115
Guess the shape.
Close your eyes. Someone, or your other hand, gives you a lid, a spoon, or a ball. Name it.

45
00:21:02,165 --> 00:22:01,032
Five pairs.
Find two things of the same color. Put them together. If you can, make another pair.

46
00:22:01,082 --> 00:22:59,950
The eye rests.
Look at one color in the picture for three breaths. Then blink.

47
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,740
Language begins in the ear. Before reading, we listen for the first sound of things.

48
00:23:06,790 --> 00:23:15,450
Your name has a door. The first letter is that door. Trace it in the air, slowly, left to right.

49
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:25,150
I spy something that starts like maaaaa. In Spanish: mesa, mano, mamá. Stretch the sound like a rubber band.

50
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:33,430
Three words of light: sun, sea, and peace. They are short, and they fit whole inside the mouth.

51
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:43,630
Syllables are a word's footsteps. Pa-per. Win-dow. Hou-se. One clap for each step.

52
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:49,970
Some words are said softly because they are a gift: thank you, please, good morning.

53
00:23:50,020 --> 00:23:56,500
A tiny poem: the sun opens the door, the river tells a story, the house says come in.

54
00:23:56,550 --> 00:24:05,810
Name things precisely. Do not only say that. Say: pitcher, rug, bead, leaf, silence.

55
00:24:05,860 --> 00:25:05,077
The door of your name.
Say your name. Stretch only the first sound. Write it in the air.

56
00:25:05,127 --> 00:26:04,345
I spy.
Find something that starts with the sound m. Touch it and say its full name.

57
00:26:04,395 --> 00:27:03,612
Sun, sea, peace.
Say the three words. For each one, count the sounds on your fingers.

58
00:27:03,662 --> 00:28:02,880
Footsteps of a word.
Clap the syllables of house, of window, and of your name.

59
00:28:02,930 --> 00:29:02,147
Gift words.
Whisper thank you to someone with you, or to your own hands.

60
00:29:02,197 --> 00:30:01,415
The poem, standing up.
Repeat: the sun opens the door. Invent the second line yourself.

61
00:30:01,465 --> 00:31:00,682
Five exact names.
Point to five objects and say each true name, without saying thing.

62
00:31:00,732 --> 00:31:59,950
One word to keep.
Choose the loveliest word from this part and say it once more, very clearly.

63
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:08,250
Mathematics in the Children's House can be touched. A number does not live only in the mouth: it lives in quantity.

64
00:32:08,300 --> 00:32:16,550
Number rods grow one by one. The shortest is one. Each step adds a red or a blue length.

65
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:22,310
One golden bead is a unit. Ten units hug and become a ten-bar.

66
00:32:22,360 --> 00:32:32,220
Ten bars make a hundred square. Ten squares make a thousand cube. Big, isn't it? And it began as one.

67
00:32:32,270 --> 00:32:40,910
Zero is the empty hand. It is not a mistake. It is the quantity of nothing, and it is a number too.

68
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:51,970
Even and odd. If everyone has a partner, the number is even. If one is left over, it is odd. Your hands can prove it.

69
00:32:52,020 --> 00:33:01,450
Counting the room is household science. Windows, chairs, lamps. One finger for each thing, skipping none.

70
00:33:01,500 --> 00:33:08,820
After counting, put the beads away. The number stays in memory, not scattered on the floor.

71
00:33:08,870 --> 00:34:15,211
From one to ten.
Count ten soft claps. If you get lost, return to one calmly.

72
00:34:15,261 --> 00:35:21,602
From short to long.
Order pencils, spoons, or books from shortest to longest.

73
00:35:21,652 --> 00:36:27,994
One and ten.
Set down one seed, button, or stone. Then make a group of ten.

74
00:36:28,044 --> 00:37:34,385
The empty hand.
Show zero with an open empty hand. Say: zero.

75
00:37:34,435 --> 00:38:40,776
Pairs.
Match pairs of socks, lids, or claps. Was one left over? Then that group is odd.

76
00:38:40,826 --> 00:39:47,168
Count the house.
Count the windows you see. Then the chairs. Say both numbers.

77
00:39:47,218 --> 00:40:53,559
Five.
Take five steps. On the fifth, stop and say: five.

78
00:40:53,609 --> 00:41:59,950
Putting away is part of the number.
If you used objects, count them again as you put them away.

79
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,960
Culture is looking out at the world without leaving respect at the door. The planet is a house too.

80
00:42:07,010 --> 00:42:15,740
Continents are great pieces of land. Oceans are the water that holds them. Land and water, both.

81
00:42:15,790 --> 00:42:25,510
A plant has root, stem, leaf, flower, and sometimes fruit. Each part works. Just like in the classroom.

82
00:42:25,560 --> 00:42:34,170
Animals have homes: the nest, the burrow, the river, the hive. We have ours, and we care for it.

83
00:42:34,220 --> 00:42:43,190
If you live near the desert, the sun, the river, and the mountains are neighbors. If not, the same sun still finds you.

84
00:42:43,240 --> 00:42:51,570
Day is for work. Night is for rest. The Earth turns, and that is why the light goes walking.

85
00:42:51,620 --> 00:42:57,950
Caring for the planet is like caring for the shelf: use what you need and leave it better than you found it.

86
00:42:58,000 --> 00:43:05,990
In another country, a child is also rolling a rug. A different language. The same care.

87
00:43:06,040 --> 00:43:57,735
Land and water.
In the picture, point to land and then water. Say both words.

88
00:43:57,785 --> 00:44:49,480
Parts of a plant.
If there is a plant, point to a leaf and a stem. If not, draw them in the air: root, stem, leaf, flower.

89
00:44:49,530 --> 00:45:41,225
An animal home.
Name an animal and its home. Bird and nest. Fish and water. Bee and hive.

90
00:45:41,275 --> 00:46:32,970
What you see outside.
Look out the window or imagine your street. Name three things from nature.

91
00:46:33,020 --> 00:47:24,715
Day and night.
Open your hands: day. Close them gently: night. Three times.

92
00:47:24,765 --> 00:48:16,460
Leave it better.
Pick up one thing that is out of place. One is enough.

93
00:48:16,510 --> 00:49:08,205
A greeting to the world.
Say hello in your language and, if you know it, in another. Hello. Hola.

94
00:49:08,255 --> 00:49:59,950
The big house.
Walk a slow circle. That circle is you caring for your small piece of the world.

95
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:07,700
Grace and courtesy is the art of living together. It is practiced, the way pouring water is practiced.

96
00:50:07,750 --> 00:50:18,380
Greeting is looking, smiling, and saying the name if you know it. Hello, Luna. Hello, Amber. Hello, you.

97
00:50:18,430 --> 00:50:26,970
Walking on the line teaches balance. One foot in front of the other. Eyes forward, not down in fear.

98
00:50:27,020 --> 00:50:34,890
You can carry a bell without letting it sing. That is control. Silence is a movement too.

99
00:50:34,940 --> 00:50:43,870
The silence game: we listen together. If you hear a noise, you do not have to catch it. Let it pass.

100
00:50:43,920 --> 00:50:53,110
Please open the door. Thank you for the glass. Excuse me, I need to pass. They are small keys.

101
00:50:53,160 --> 00:51:01,680
When someone is working, we walk around the rug. We do not step on it. It is their country for a while.

102
00:51:01,730 --> 00:51:07,990
And at the end, we thank the people and the materials. Both of them helped.

103
00:51:08,040 --> 00:51:56,650
A complete greeting.
Look at someone, smile, and say their name, or say: hello, good morning.

104
00:51:56,700 --> 00:52:45,310
The line on the floor.
If you can, place a tape on the floor. Walk on it slowly, there and back.

105
00:52:45,360 --> 00:53:33,970
The quiet bell.
Carry a spoon or keys in your palm while walking, without making them sound.

106
00:53:34,020 --> 00:54:22,630
A silence of ten.
With an adult, be quiet together while you count ten breaths. Then one smile.

107
00:54:22,680 --> 00:55:11,290
Walk around the rug.
Imagine a rectangle on the floor. Walk around the outside. Never cross it.

108
00:55:11,340 --> 00:55:59,950
Three keys.
Say: please, thank you, excuse me. A tiny bow at the end, if you want.

109
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:09,530
The hour is put away, the way work is put away. Slowly. With care. Leaving nothing scattered.

110
00:56:09,580 --> 00:56:17,710
Look at the shelf of your memory. What did you keep today? A word, a number, or a soft step.

111
00:56:17,760 --> 00:56:27,980
Thank you, hands. Thank you, eyes. Thank you, ears. You worked the whole hour and did not complain.

112
00:56:28,030 --> 00:56:35,610
We sing softly: quiet hands, happy heart. See you soon, little children's house.

113
00:56:35,660 --> 00:56:44,560
Whether outside there is desert sun or rain in another city, it does not matter. You already put something in order inside.

114
00:56:44,610 --> 00:56:52,700
The last step is the most elegant. Walk toward the person who cares for you and say: I finished my hour.

115
00:56:52,750 --> 00:57:00,240
This was reinforcement, not a race. Your guide at school is still the one who walks with you each day.

116
00:57:00,290 --> 00:57:09,220
Until the next fun hour. I, Amber, stay shining on the shelf. You may go and play the silence.

117
00:57:09,270 --> 00:57:37,675
What did you keep?
Say one thing you remember from this hour. Only one, well said.

118
00:57:37,725 --> 00:58:06,130
The short song.
Sing or say: quiet hands, happy heart. See you soon, little children's house.

119
00:58:06,180 --> 00:58:34,585
Thanks in three.
Touch your hands, your eyes, and your ears, and say thank you to each.

120
00:58:34,635 --> 00:59:03,040
The sun at your window.
Look at the light. Say whether it is sun, cloud, or lamp. Name it with respect.

121
00:59:03,090 --> 00:59:31,495
The last step.
Walk to your adult and say: I finished my hour.

122
00:59:31,545 --> 00:59:59,950
Final silence.
Stay quiet for one long breath. The hour rests with you.
